 - Windows: see the tables above. The evidence directory contains no full canary value and no user name, host
   name or home path. Placeholders are `<scratch>`, `<repo>`, `<home>` and `S-1-5-21-<redacted>`.
+
+## 17. Bug fix: symlinked `--file` rejected (X2 task T4)
+
+**Report.** `profile show --file <link>` (with and without `--json`) and `tui --file <link>` exited 2
+`USAGE_ERROR` "profile path is not a regular file" when the path was a symbolic link (absolute or relative)
+to an ordinary profile, e.g. a dotfiles/GNU stow layout.
+
+**Cause.** `profile::read_bounded` ran a pre-open check with `std::fs::symlink_metadata`, which does not
+follow a final symlink, so the link itself (file type "symlink") failed the regular-file test before the
+file was ever opened. The comment justified this as a TOCTOU guard (a link retargeted to a FIFO between check
+and open), but that guard was redundant: the authoritative K14 check is already on the opened descriptor
+(`O_NONBLOCK` open, then `fstat`; `GetFileType` on Windows), which cannot be raced. The shared reference
+implementation (`tests/g02/reference_impl.py` `load_profile_file`) also follows links and decides on `fstat`.
+Round 3b's `k14_non_regular_profile_files` had pinned the wrong behavior (link to a regular file → exit 2).
+
+**Fix** (`src/profile.rs`).
+- The pre-open check uses `std::fs::metadata` (follows links, like the open does). It stays only as an
+  optimisation: a FIFO/device/socket/directory behind the path, directly or via any chain of links, is
+  normally rejected without being opened. Unresolvable paths (missing, dangling link, loop, permission) fall
+  through to the open, which reports `USAGE_ERROR` "cannot open profile file: <kind>" as before.
+- Unchanged and still authoritative: the non-blocking open plus descriptor check (K14, §9.6). A path swapped to
+  a FIFO or device after the pre-check is still rejected without blocking.
+- Hardening: the Unix open adds `O_NOCTTY`. Following links means a link can now lead to a terminal device;
+  in the race window above it must never become the controlling terminal before the `fstat` rejects it.
+
+**Tests.** Red proofs actually run against pre-fix builds: `symlinked_profile_reads_like_its_target`
+(darwin, fails), `tui-symlinked-profile` (darwin and linux-arm64, fails), and the report's reproduction
+(linux-arm64, exit 2). The K14 link cases pass on both builds by design (they guard the fix from widening
+K14). The unit test was not run against the pre-fix code.
+- `tests/cli.rs` `symlinked_profile_reads_like_its_target`: absolute link, relative `../dotfiles/x.toml`
+  link, two-hop chain and a file reached through a symlinked directory give byte-identical stdout, stderr and
+  exit status to the real file, for a valid (`PROFILE_OK`) and an invalid (`SCHEMA_INVALID`) profile, with and
+  without `--json`; a dangling link and a link loop are exit 2 `USAGE_ERROR`.
+- `tests/cli.rs` `k14_non_regular_profile_files`: the old "link to a regular file is refused" assertion is
+  removed; links (absolute, relative, chained) to the FIFO, directory, `/dev/null` and socket are added and
+  must each be exit 2 `USAGE_ERROR` within 2 s.
+- `src/profile.rs` unit test `symlink_to_regular_file_loads_like_the_file` (library level, same cases plus a
+  link to a FIFO and to a directory).
+- `tests/pty_tui.py` case `tui-symlinked-profile`: `tui` opens the profile through an absolute and a relative
+  link and quits with exit 0 and a restored terminal; a link to a FIFO is exit 2 in under 2 s with no
+  alternate screen.
+
+**Not covered natively.** Windows symlinks (`mklink`) were not exercised: no Windows host in this round. The
+Windows code path changes only in the same way (the pre-check now follows the link; `GetFileType` after the
+open is unchanged), and `windows-x64` still builds.
